    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is there a sat nav for horse riders?</summary>
        <p>Yes. BridleNav is a GPS navigation app built for horseback rather than for a car or for walking. It speaks turn-by-turn directions out loud so you can keep both hands on the reins and your phone in your pocket.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does BridleNav work without a phone signal?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Download the map before you box up and the app keeps navigating with no signal at all. Riders have completed whole loops on BridleNav with no reception. The SOS feature uses GPS to find you, though sending the message needs a signal.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How is it different from a walking or cycling app?</summary>
        <p>Walking and cycling apps send you down footpaths and canal towpaths where horses are not allowed, and they expect you to look at a screen. BridleNav routes are bridleways and byways, and everything is spoken aloud.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which parts of the UK does BridleNav cover?</summary>
        <p>The routes we have ridden and written up ourselves are in the Peak District, Derbyshire, Cheshire, Lancashire, Staffordshire and the Lake District. Riders anywhere in the UK can record and share their own routes, so the map grows wherever riders are.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I add my own routes?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Record a ride on your phone, then at home write the turn-by-turn directions in your own words and mark the gates, water crossings and livestock. Every submission is read before it is published, and you choose whether your name appears.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does BridleNav cost?</summary>
        <p>Your first complete ride is free with everything switched on. After that it is &pound;10.99 a month or &pound;99.99 a year, with a seven-day free trial. Subscriptions are handled by the App Store and Google Play and you can cancel there at any time.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it safe to use a phone while riding?</summary>
        <p>BridleNav is designed so you do not have to. The screen can be off and the phone in your pocket; the app talks to you. If you have to look at it, it has not worked.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
